<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Samara Bend</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1223</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongol-invasion-of-volga-bulgaria">Mongol invasion of Volga Bulgaria</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Samara Bend was fought in 1223 near the great bend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> at Samara, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, when the Volga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> ambushed part of the Mongol army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subutai">Subutai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jebe">Jebe</a> returning from its victory on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalka">Kalka</a> River. Medieval sources report heavy Mongol losses. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> returned under Batu and conquered Volga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> in 1236.</p></div>
